The `themes/` directory sits next to the resolved `config.toml` (see `tui::theme::file::themes_dir_for_config`), and is discovered at startup. Files named `dark.toml` or `light.toml` override the corresponding built-ins, and any other `<name>.toml` adds a selectable theme — no rebuild needed. The config's `theme` key selects a theme by name (default is `dark`) — unknown names will fail to load — the CLI `--theme` flag overrides it per run, the "Theme" item in the menu opens a picker that lists all discovered themes, and Ctrl+S cycles through all of them in discovery order: existing lines are restyled in place (prompt lines take the prompt style, reasoning lines are reconstructed with edges and tints, and everything else takes the panel background), while text, Markdown spans, and code highlights remain unchanged.
```

