    feat(engine): add theming, scrollbar pager and compact prompt layout
    
    - Semantic light/dark themes with a process-wide theme registry and
      NO_COLOR/CLICOLOR/CLICOLOR_FORCE awareness; resolution falls back
      through KVIST_THEME, .kvist/theme, ~/.config/kvist/theme and an OSC 11
      terminal background probe before defaulting to dark.
    - User-customizable themes via a bounded, validated TOML spec file.
    - The 'theme' builtin lists and previews every theme live and persists
      the selection atomically to .kvist/theme.
    - Full-screen scroll pager for output with a right-edge scrollbar sized
      proportionally to the document, replacing the minus dependency.
    - Working and result output merge into one integrated agent box with a
      true-black result surface by default, and the double border between
      output and prompt becomes a single rule line with badge-aware key
      hints that drop whole groups instead of truncating mid-line.

