- Idempotent: no-op (never touches the network) when the registry already satisfies the lock.
- When the lockfile drifted: runs `cargo vendor` — the host-authorized, bounded acquisition step — *before* the effect sandbox is created. The sandbox itself remains network-denied, per your constraint.
- Fail-closed preserved: if the reconcile can't complete (e.g. no network and a crate missing), it fails with an actionable message instead of a cryptic `chrono` resolution error.

